//// emilia — CSS-in-bp for botopink/jhonstart (intent skeleton).
////
//// This file is the placeholder body declared by `root.bp`'s `pub default mod
//// emilia;`. The real runtime (the `EmiliaClass` record, `styled` namespace,
//// `css """…"""` + `tw "…"` template fns, and the `Stylesheet` host-cell
//// seam) is implemented across the F1–F5 steps of
//// `tasks/v0.beta.19/specs/emilia.md` in the parent workspace.
////
//// Until then, the only published symbol is a sentinel `version` constant —
//// enough for `from "emilia"` to resolve in a consumer and for `botopink test`
//// to see a module that compiles. The empty surface is deliberate: the spec
//// is INTENT, immutable once written, and seed commits ship only what is
//// strictly needed for the workspace to wire emilia as a submodule.

pub val version = "0.0.1";
